Subject: [PATCH] media: the persona's device list replaces the host's

enumerateDevices() lists the persona's microphones, cameras and speakers
and nothing else. Until now the persona's counts were a floor: the
host's devices stayed listed under their own names and groups, and only
the shortfall was made up, so a Windows persona on a Mac listed the
Mac's microphone by name after a permission grant.

The list is the same on every host. What opens is worked out from the
host each time: device i opens host device i, a microphone beyond the
host's count opens the host's first one, a camera beyond it is the
synthetic camera, since one host camera cannot be opened twice, and
every speaker plays on the host's default output. With no host device
of a kind, the existing synthetic devices serve. The default and, for a
Windows persona, communications entries carry the persona's first
device and open the host's default.

A persona whose machine has no microphone or no camera lists one, named
from its machine class, when the host has one, so calls keep working.

An open track agrees with the list: its label is the persona's, a
microphone reports the persona's sample rate, channels and buffer, and
a camera offers the sizes of its persona class that the host camera
has, at up to 30 fps, with no pan, tilt or zoom and the persona's
photo state.

